#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
zorca-gui2 - the ZAO orchestration dashboard, redesigned. Local only.

Decisions first: one NEEDS-YOU rail (gates, drafts, panes that asked you
something), then the wall, then everything else behind a fold. The count
can reach zero, and zero is rendered as a win.

Implements research doc 2420 (SPEC.md). Runs on 7778 so the original
zorca-gui on 7777 stays up for side-by-side comparison.

One file, stdlib only. Serves a live board at http://127.0.0.1:7778 over
YOUR state: Orca panes (via orca-board --json), the orchestration Run's
tasks and decision gates (via the orca CLI). Gates are answered by tapping
an option - the tap runs `orca orchestration gate-resolve`, nothing else.

Never exposed off-localhost. Never touches Orca's code. Reads state, and
the only writes it can do are the ones Zaal taps: resolve a gate, focus a
pane.

Run:  zorca-gui2           (then open http://127.0.0.1:7778)
      zorca-gui2 --port N
"""
